  "slug": "bacterial-fitness-calibration-evo2-0f95",
  "summary": "Pretrained biological foundation models are now being tested for contamination, reproducibility and external performance, not only in-house accuracy.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is learned representations of omics and pathology data, increasingly built from pretrained or distilled encoders and evaluated for trustworthiness. scVision renders single-cell transcriptomes as images and pretrains a vision transformer on 72 million human cells, while GigaPath-Flash and GigaTIME-Flash distil tile and LongNet slide encoders to predict tumor immune microenvironment features. What is new is scrutiny of these models. scContam combines MinHash gene-set fingerprinting with loss-based membership inference to detect pretraining contamination in single-cell foundation model benchmarks. A pre-registered external evaluation of Geneformer, scGPT and UCE on Replogle Perturb-seq (RPE1, K562) reports that all three beat controls yet yields a consistent partial-replication outcome. Minmax-CF selects real cells and genes for traceable data distillation, and a blood-cell pipeline routes frozen ConceptCLIP morphological concept scores through a soft decision tree for interpretability.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-07-21"
}
